<?xml version="1.0" standalone="yes"?>

<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name      "smb-restart">
<!ENTITY author    "Maxwell Luong">
<!ENTITY version   "2026.07.25.4">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/maxandcheeses/unraid-restart-smb/main/smb-restart.plg">
<!-- The .txz is attached as a GitHub Release asset (tag vVERSION), not committed to main. -->
<!ENTITY pkgURL    "https://github.com/maxandcheeses/unraid-restart-smb/releases/download/v&version;/&name;-&version;-noarch.txz">
<!ENTITY pkgMD5    "6e96125688c4b38e5cf2b93f7b67cc27">
]>

<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" pluginURL="&pluginURL;" icon="images/smb-restart.png" min="6.9.0">

  <CHANGES>
###&version;
- Fix nav-item icon: resize to 16x16 (was 128x128, wildly oversized for the
  topbar) and switch to a colored disc glyph matching the convention used by
  Unraid's own icons (e.g. the power button), instead of a large flat
  black-on-white square.
- Add Code="f021" (fontawesome refresh icon) so the button still renders via
  Unraid's CSS ::before font-icon path at wide viewports (1330px+), where
  Unraid hides the image icon entirely and requires a Code-based icon instead.

###2026.07.25.3
- Replace the core-file-patching topbar hack with the real mechanism Unraid
  provides: a Menu="Buttons" page (SmbRestart.page), which renders as an
  actual nav-item button next to search/notifications/logout — the same way
  Unraid's own power button works. No patched core files anymore.

###2026.07.25.2
- Fix topbar-injection target and stop shipping macOS AppleDouble junk files
  (superseded by the 2026.07.25.3 rewrite above).

###2026.07.25.1
- Add plugin icon (shown on the Plugins page) and repo description.

###2026.07.25
- Initial release: restart/start SMB via a Tools page and a topbar status icon.
  </CHANGES>

  <FILE Name="/boot/config/plugins/&name;/&name;-&version;-noarch.txz" Min="6.9.0">
    <URL>&pkgURL;</URL>
    <MD5>&pkgMD5;</MD5>
  </FILE>

  <FILE Run="/bin/bash">
    <INLINE>
upgradepkg --install-new --reinstall /boot/config/plugins/&name;/&name;-&version;-noarch.txz
    </INLINE>
  </FILE>

  <FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
    <INLINE>
removepkg &name;-&version;-noarch
rm -rf /boot/config/plugins/&name;
    </INLINE>
  </FILE>

</PLUGIN>
